# VEILRUN — things that should never land in the repo.
# Keep this tight: the site is deployed straight from git, so anything ignored
# here is also absent from the live build.

# --- macOS / Finder noise ---
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# --- Windows noise (in case anyone else clones) ---
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- FUSE tombstones ---
# Created when a mounted process holds a file open while something else rewrites
# it (agent sessions working in this repo). Empty artifacts, never content.
.fuse_hidden*

# --- Editor / tooling ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# --- Agent config: ALL OF IT (VR-164, 9/5) ---
# THIS REPO IS THE PUBLIC WEBSITE and Cloudflare Pages serves dot-directories
# like any other. Verified 9/5: .claude/agents/release-steward.md returned live
# content at https://veilrun-dxv.pages.dev/.claude/agents/release-steward.md —
# it had been world-readable since the day it was committed.
#
# Only `.claude/settings.local.json` was ignored before, which reads as "agent
# config is handled" and is why nobody looked again. Skills, agents, commands
# and hooks are internal process: they name unshipped cards, quote Jordan, and
# describe how the project is run. None of it is dangerous; all of it is ours.
#
# The whole directory is ignored rather than a list of subfolders, because a
# list only covers the kinds of agent config that exist today. `.gitignore`
# does NOT untrack what is already tracked — see the VR-164 card for that.
.claude/

# --- Local dev servers & scratch ---
# Local-only helper scripts (e.g. a python http.server launcher for playtesting
# the 3D builds). Keep these OUTSIDE the repo where possible.
_serve.command
*.local.command
/scratch/
/tmp/

# --- Secrets ---
# The Supabase anon/publishable key is browser-safe and lives in js/config.js on
# purpose. The service_role key must NEVER be committed, in any form.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*secret*
*service_role*

# --- Dependencies / build output ---
# There is no build step today (every game is a standalone single file), but if
# one is ever added this stops the output being committed by accident.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.cache/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# --- Agent observability (STU-02 / STU-03) ---
# claude-office and the studio event log both write OUTSIDE this repo by design
# (~/.claude/ and ~/Documents/GitHub/claude-office/). These patterns exist only
# so that a future tool writing cwd-relative cannot leak tool I/O or file paths
# into a repo that is served verbatim. Belt and braces — nothing matches today.
*.jsonl
agent-events/
visualizer.db
visualizer.db-wal
visualizer.db-shm
claude-office-hooks.log
